{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1538196-what-if-malfeas-as-a-prison-realm-disconnected-from-creation","id":1538196,"title":"What if Malfeas as a Prison Realm disconnected from Creation?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-06T22:25:15-07:00","id":1538196,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> What if Malfeas as a Prison Realm disconnected from Creation?","content":"For a not Exalted game I'm running in 1100 AD &quot;Mythic&quot; Medieval Europe using the Ars Magica Ruleset; the PC Order of Hermes Magi are discovering Malfeas and simply know it as the &quot;Prison of Forever&quot; and initially believed Atlantian sorcerers constructed it, but instead recently discovered the Atlantians found this realm in &quot;Elsewhere.&quot;<br /> <br /> **all **of the Yozi's inside Malfeas have fallen asleep. Their component souls also are mostly in a rested state. The Atlantians found that Malfeas had been undisturbed for thousands of years, and so began to use it as a prison, which awoke a single component soul of Malfeas, but little else. (So I'm borrowing Exalted Lore into my Ars Magica game)<br /> <br /> What could have happened for Malfeas to have:<br /> <br /> (1) Become disconnected from Creation<br /> AND<br /> (2) Caused the Yozi's within Malfeas, all component souls, even all the 1st circle demons to fall asleep, and not wake up?<br /> <br /> Myself I am picturing a Creation that was destroyed, or possibly another catastrophic event happened. Open to any and all ideas out there.<br /> <br /> Edited due to @<b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\">Baaldam</a></b>'s questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 03-18-2025, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-07T01:54:11-07:00","id":1538199,"title":"","content":"Someone figured out a way to invert the Divine Ignition so Cytheria ended up replicating her waking of all her kin by being the lullaby which puts them all to sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-29T15:36:59-08:00","id":1548037,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>In response to the failed attempt of Return the Scarlet Empress (she got thunderbolted the moment she entered Creation as Yu Shan found out about the plan) the Celestial Exalted were gathered to charge a sorcery that not only banished the Yozis further away but put them to sleep.</li> <li>Creation is no more due to the Neverborn or Fair Folk winning, and so the Yozi disconnected themselves and put themselves to sleep to preserve valuable essence.</li> <li>Autochton woke up and decided to poison all of Malfeas to slumber to eat their dreams as a renewable energy source.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-30T17:21:32-08:00","id":1548076,"title":"","content":"The games broke down, essence in creation dried up, and all the Yozi fell into slumber due to the lack of essence with the oaths cutting them off from the wyld and now creation empty of essence they just float through elsewhere just waiting to connect with a new realm to use as a new energy source to start awakening again (the process to wake up is exactly as slow or fast as your game needs it to be lol)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-31T17:19:22-08:00","id":1548101,"title":"","content":"You can adapt the old (if never really official) &quot;exalted turned into the world we live in now&quot; idea, and sprinkle it with the Autochthon's situation - just pushed much further.<br /> <br /> It did not really become disconnected. It was <i>always</i> out there, the way inside was simply forgotten throughout all the transformations the world went through since.<br /> When all the channels connecting Demon City to Creation were closed, the essence levels started dropping lowe and lower. Malfeas, and the other Yozis started to slumber for longer and longer in order to stretch their reserves for longer, and eventually went completely asleep, waiting for the problem to go away. Unfortunately for them, when situation deteriorated further, demons they left in charge were affected as well. First it happened to Third circles, then the Second circles went to sleep as well. Eventually, the first circles also succumbed (well, those that did not simply die away before that point).<br /> Now, that the doors have been opened again, the essence started to trickle in, drawing more and more of the inhabitants closer to the awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-05T07:08:37-08:00","id":1548221,"title":"","content":"Great suggestions, thank you guys, keep them coming!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-05T15:15:47-08:00","id":1548994,"title":"","content":"Not gonna lie, you kind of lost me somewhere between &quot;Ars Magica&quot; and &quot;Atlantian sorcerers&quot; - i got mostly back, but still kind of confused overall.<br /> <br /> Are you playing with Ars Magica per se and some of its concepts and mechanics or the setting ported to some version of the Storyteller system, like Mage: the Ascension, Sorcerer's Crusade, Awakening or some variant that i forget?<br /> <br /> Because depending on the answer i'll probably have some further questions about what is going on and thoughts on possible weird bits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-18T14:38:01-07:00","id":1549418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1538196-what-if-malfeas-as-a-prison-realm-disconnected-from-creation?p=1548994#post1548994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not gonna lie, you kind of lost me somewhere between &quot;Ars Magica&quot; and &quot;Atlantian sorcerers&quot; - i got mostly back, but still kind of confused overall.<br /> <br /> Are you playing with Ars Magica per se and some of its concepts and mechanics or the setting ported to some version of the Storyteller system, like Mage: the Ascension, Sorcerer's Crusade, Awakening or some variant that i forget?<br /> <br /> Because depending on the answer i'll probably have some further questions about what is going on and thoughts on possible weird bits.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, game is set in 1100 AD in &quot;Mythic&quot; Medieval Europe using the Ars Magica rules to run the game. I am borrowing Lore from Exalted, specifically the prison realm Malfeas. The ancient Sorcerers of Atlantis rediscovered Malfeas using dimensional magic. These sorcerers found Malfeas mostly &quot;asleep&quot; and the Demons harder to summon. Why was and is this still the case?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-15T17:58:26-07:00","id":1551057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1538196-what-if-malfeas-as-a-prison-realm-disconnected-from-creation?p=1549418#post1549418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, game is set in 1100 AD in &quot;Mythic&quot; Medieval Europe using the Ars Magica rules to run the game. I am borrowing Lore from Exalted, specifically the prison realm Malfeas. The ancient Sorcerers of Atlantis rediscovered Malfeas using dimensional magic. These sorcerers found Malfeas mostly &quot;asleep&quot; and the Demons harder to summon. Why was and is this still the case?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ancient Sorcerers of Atlantis? dimensional magic (re)discovering Malfeas?<br /> <br /> Sincerely, from what i remember of Ars Magica (older editions admitedly) the hermetic mages interactions with demons were.... fraught, to say the least and not even sure they could quite summon those, for that matter. And Atlantis had little to nothing to do with the Order, its history or magic, for that matter.<br /> <br /> Honestly, i'm more uncertain now of what is going on in your game than i was when i first asked. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-15-2025, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-25T11:33:44-07:00","id":1551271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1538196-what-if-malfeas-as-a-prison-realm-disconnected-from-creation?p=1551057#post1551057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ancient Sorcerers of Atlantis? dimensional magic (re)discovering Malfeas?<br /> <br /> Sincerely, from what i remember of Ars Magica (older editions admitedly) the hermetic mages interactions with demons were.... fraught, to say the least and not even sure they could quite summon those, for that matter. And Atlantis had little to nothing to do with the Order, its history or magic, for that matter.<br /> <br /> Honestly, i'm more uncertain now of what is going on in your game than i was when i first asked. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's okay man, just relax. I'm running a very Non-Traditional Ars Magica game. Most games run like Downton Abby. Mine has run more like a campaign of Sith Lords' genocidal invasion of the Jedi and terrorizing the survivors.<br /> <br /> Why does Atlantis have to have anything to do with the Order? It doesn't. I'm just explaining WHY Malfeas is a thing in my Ars Magica game. This is all just background explanations.<br /> <br /> Here's a write up to my first 35 or so sessions of a 91 session campaign.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/actual-play-write-up-1st-crusade-campaign-of-1096/170538/7\" target=\"_blank\">Actual Play Write Up: 1st Crusade Campaign of 1096 - Games Discussion / Ars Magica - Atlas Games RPG Forum</a><br /> <br /> Overall, I'm just looking for reasons in Exalted on why or how Malfeas became detached from Creation and began to float in Elsewhere for eons, causing Malfeas and inhabitants to fall asleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 05-25-2025, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-25T15:56:53-07:00","id":1551278,"title":"","content":"So I'm not 100% sure, but I would note that somewhere in the gameline it was stated that the Incarnae deliberately chose not to sever Malfeas and the other Yozis from Creation and its environs entirely on purpose, as this would have made the fallen makers of the world enraged beyond their current state and they really would have laid waste to everything with no care for what happened to themselves; The Three Spheres Cataclysm that permanently broke the perfect symmetry of the Principle of Hierarchy and scoured the world would look like a tapped funny bone next to what they would have been willing to endure then.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that what you're asking is a bad idea. Just that whatever happened would at least within the bounds of canon (which we have already clearly stepped beyond) not have been deliberate.<br /> <br /> *shrugs*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-31T21:01:40-07:00","id":1551376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1538196-what-if-malfeas-as-a-prison-realm-disconnected-from-creation?p=1551278#post1551278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm not 100% sure, but I would note that somewhere in the gameline it was stated that the Incarnae deliberately chose not to sever Malfeas and the other Yozis from Creation and its environs entirely on purpose, as this would have made the fallen makers of the world enraged beyond their current state and they really would have laid waste to everything with no care for what happened to themselves; The Three Spheres Cataclysm that permanently broke the perfect symmetry of the Principle of Hierarchy and scoured the world would look like a tapped funny bone next to what they would have been willing to endure then.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that what you're asking is a bad idea. Just that whatever happened would at least within the bounds of canon (which we have already clearly stepped beyond) not have been deliberate.<br /> <br /> *shrugs*</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good point. So what happened after the fact that severed Malfeas from creation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-01T06:58:46-07:00","id":1551386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1538196-what-if-malfeas-as-a-prison-realm-disconnected-from-creation?p=1551376#post1551376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a good point. So what happened after the fact that severed Malfeas from creation?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>And then the Demon City, the Demon King, with no room to turn His wrath and despair<br /> Turned them upon His peers, who in turn raged, raged, raged against each other.<br /> For the turning of ages did Their mindless, boundless violence scour across the whole of their prison<br /> The Unquestionable raised their greater selves' fury woven into banners of war, marching on each other<br /> Whole nations rose and died, grew and died, made war and died. <br /> Death was the only constant, though denied to the Yozis themselves.<br /> <br /> And then, when the Age had turned, and turned again, when Their Creation was bent<br /> Their rage not spent<br /> For what is boundless can never run dry<br /> But Their throats scoured dry from screaming<br /> And Their forms weary from thrashing<br /> Did the Yozis turn for a time to slumber</i><br /> <br /> (They throw a tantrum until they pass out until, presumably, the present)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}